<title>JAPAN: Bank of Japan drains 600 bln yen from market.</title>
<headline>Bank of Japan drains 600 bln yen from market.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Japan (BOJ) drained a net 600 billion yen from the money market on Friday, money traders said.</p>
<p>The drainage almost balanced out a net market surplus of an estimated 610 billion yen for the day. Today is the last day of the current bank reserve reporting period.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8570</p>
</text>
